      "smallPath": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-8-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "臺北刑務所圍牆近景.jpg",
      "title": "File:臺北刑務所圍牆近景.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/94/%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E5%88%91%E5%8B%99%E6%89%80%E5%9C%8D%E7%89%86%E8%BF%91%E6%99%AF.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E5%88%91%E5%8B%99%E6%89%80%E5%9C%8D%E7%89%86%E8%BF%91%E6%99%AF.jpg",
      "width": 3424,
      "height": 3424,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "氏子",
      "description": "Each layer of bricks was laid through stretcher-header bonds. The outer course of headers and the inner course of stretchers intersected in a \"T\" shape, and the inner course of headers and the outer course of stretchers also intersected in a \"T\" shape. The construction method ensured that the inner and outer course of bricks were laid with \"grooves\" and \"staggered joints\" to form a stable structure in which each layer of bricks was interconnected. \"Stucco paint\" made of granulated sugar and lime was also used to bond the bricks firmly.",
      "dateCreated": "2023-03-12 16:27:58",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "wsqq",
      "mediumPath": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-9-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-9-small.webp"
    },
